    "description": "In this video, Nicole shows you how to make prize winning baby back ribs at your next cookout. With a sweet and spicy homemade rub made with chili powder and brown sugar, coat both sides of the ribs. Using either a gas or charcoal grill, let the ribs cook from the indirect heat for around two hours before coating them in barbecue sauce. Elevate your next backyard barbecue with these smokey, tender, and delicious baby back ribs!",
